T-835-BLUF [ec554439421e] Landed on main: pull request 233 makes every CSV the dashboard downloads write a cell that a spreadsheet would read as a formula as text. One shared function, csvCell (static/js/index.js line 124), now writes the cell of all ten CSV writers (the eight export closures, the recent prints export and the AI reply export, so two more than the eight this ticket counted): a value whose first character is an equals sign, a plus sign, a minus sign, an at sign, a tab or a carriage return gets a single quote in front of it, inside the quotes. A plain number (digits, an optional sign, one decimal point, an optional percent sign) and a run of dashes (the empty-cell marker) are left as they were, which is the answer to this ticket's open question about numeric columns that start with a minus sign. This ticket's fix shape (one shared helper, cells for each export path, a plant that drops the prefix reddens them) is met by the change, as the independent review measured: it attacked the helper with 62 inputs and each writer with 59, every formula-shaped input was prefixed, no input was found that an exemption lets through as a formula, the ten writers wrote 0 formula cells out of 590 in the fields the helper writes where main wrote 28 per writer, and every plant turned exactly its predicted cells red. Not claimed and left open: numeric cells that four of the writers still write without the helper, a leading space or new line before an equals sign, look-alike characters for it, the server-side exports and any run in a real spreadsheet; a follow-up is proposed. The helper's rule and its two exemptions are defaults of the change, not decisions by the product owner. <<OUTCOME>>
