T-835-Detail [06cbe9d6e0ea] <<LAND233>> This ticket's fix shape (one shared helper that puts a single quote in front of a value whose first character is an equals sign, a plus sign, a minus sign, an at sign, a tab or a carriage return; cells for each export path; a plant that drops the prefix must redden them) and its open question (numeric columns that start with a minus sign: prefix them or exempt pure numbers), read against the independent review and the builder's record. (1) The change in static/js/index.js: csvCell at line 124 (its comment starts at line 120) quotes the value, doubles its inner quotes and, when the first character is one of the six and the value is neither a plain number nor a run of dashes, puts a single quote in front of it inside the quotes. It is the cell writer of the eight export closures (the line const esc = csvCell is on 8 lines: 5850, 5910, 5924, 5951, 5964, 5992, 6004 and 6031), of the recent prints export (line 2122) and of the AI reply export (lines 3156 and 3161). This ticket counted eight paths; the other two were found since. (2) What the review measured by running the shipped helper and the ten shipped writers, with the output read by an RFC 4180 parser: 62 helper inputs and 59 per writer; every input that starts with one of the six characters, the DDE and HYPERLINK shapes, and an object and an array holding a formula, was prefixed inside the quotes; the exemption attacks (a minus sign followed by arithmetic, a function call, an equals sign, more dashes, an exponent, a trailing space or other trailing characters, or a thousands comma) were all prefixed and no input was found that an exemption lets through as a formula; the ten writers wrote 0 formula cells out of 590 (59 per writer) in the fields the helper writes, where main wrote 28 formula cells per writer (25 for the all-tabs export); a value holding a comma, a quote or a new line stayed one cell in every writer; a 200 KB value was prefixed and stayed one cell; plain number