T-445-BLUF [82416ec6c55e] Landed on main: pull request 234 makes the Marketplace webhook token check refuse the skip flag in production. In backend/marketplaceJwt.js (the flag test at line 65, the production test at line 69, the middleware from line 115), when MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT is true and NODE_ENV is production (compared trimmed and case-insensitively) the flag is ignored: the Bearer token goes to the same verification function, with the same options and the same 401 answers, as when the flag is unset, and an error line is logged when the router is built and again for every webhook request that meets the flag (fixed text: no token, header or caller value is in it). Outside production the flag works as before and now also logs one warning line when the router is built. This ticket's item 2 asked to refuse the flag when NODE_ENV is production (or remove it), to log loudly when it is on, to add a cell (production plus the flag still verifies) and to confirm that no template, compose file, workflow or document sets it. The first three are met by the change, as the independent review measured; for the fourth, the review enumerated the flag name over every tracked file and it sits in the middleware, the hand-run smoke script, the history file (twice, in notes that say it is for local use and must not be set in production) and the new test file, and in no template, compose file or workflow. Items 1, 3 and 4 of this ticket are not touched and this ticket stays open. Not claimed: an instance whose NODE_ENV is unset or is not production still skips the check when the flag is on; the new cells mock the token library, so they prove which path is taken and not a signature check. The refusal rule, the trimmed case-insensitive test, the log wording, the kept flag and the mocked library are defaults of the change, not decisions by the product owner. <<OUTCOME>>
