T-NEWG-P3 [6214c833542a] Recommendation (a proposal, not decided): add a boot-time check so that an instance that has the flag on and is not a development run does not start serving the webhook unverified: either refuse to start (or refuse to mount the Marketplace router) when MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT is true and NODE_ENV is anything but development or test, or log one FATAL line and refuse in the same form as the existing refusals. Decide the allowed values (the review's matrix shows prod, staging, empty and unset as the cases that skip today), whether the start-up check and the token check should share one production test, and whether to remove the flag altogether and have the smoke script mock the library. Cells: a start with the flag on and each non-development value is refused; a start with the flag on and NODE_ENV development starts and logs the warning; the existing cells pass. Low proposed: every shipped path sets production, no running instance is known to carry the flag, and the change already refuses it in production.
